---
import Container from "../shared/Container.astro";
import Paragraph from "../shared/Paragraph.astro";
import Title from "../shared/Title.astro";
---

<section class="relative py-16 md:py-20" id="philosophy">
    <Container className="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
        <div class="text-center space-y-4">
            <Title>
                Why Agentic Development Needs a New Foundation
            </Title>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6">
            <Paragraph>
                AI is transforming software development — but most teams are simply bolting AI tools onto existing processes. The result? Unreliable outputs, no verification, and wasted potential. <strong>Agentic development</strong> demands more than clever prompts; it requires a foundation built on determinism and designed for human-AI collaboration.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                That foundation has two pillars. First, <strong>deterministic system understanding</strong> — AI agents need a precise, repeatable map of your architecture to work effectively, not hallucinated context. Second, <strong>processes designed for the AI era</strong> — your SDLC must separate creative human decisions from autonomous AI execution, with verification at every step.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                At Noesis Vision, we deliver both. Our <strong>product</strong> creates the deterministic knowledge layer that humans and AI agents share. Our <strong>services</strong> redesign your development lifecycle to harness AI's full potential — safely, verifiably, and at scale.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
        </div>
    </Container>
</section>
